CM_ SG_ 85 BrakePedalActive2 "Active during braking";
CM_ SG_ 85 NEW_SIGNAL_1 "Not yet figured out.";
CM_ SG_ 85 BrakePedalActive "Brake pedal pushed. Behaves like a pressure threshold (~75-100 on 0x1B0 BrakePress0), not a switch.";
CM_ SG_ 8 SteeringDirection "1=Right turn, 0=Left turn. Steering wheel pointing left or right from center (0 deg).";
CM_ SG_ 8 RelativeTurnDirection "1=Right turn, 0=Left turn. Steering wheel currently turning the way.";
CM_ SG_ 101 NEW_SIGNAL_1 "Rate of something?";
CM_ SG_ 192 TransmissionGear "0 = 1st gear, 1= 2nd gear...";
CM_ SG_ 681 TurnSignal "0 = Nothing, 1= Left, 3=Right";
CM_ SG_ 681 HighBeamOn "1=HighBeam On, 0=HighBeam Off";
CM_ SG_ 48 ACCStatusTracking "ACC Tracking vehicle, distance control.";
CM_ SG_ 48 ACCStatusOnOff "Turns one after pressing on/off button on steering wheel";
CM_ SG_ 48 ACCStatusActive "ACC Active. Byte 7 of 0x30 in the dashcam route: 0x8A = ACC standby, 0x8F = active tracking, 0x8E = active no tracking, 0x9F = active (bit 4 also set), 0x88 = off. In the 15 km/h route with openpilot running it stayed 0x88 throughout, unexplained.";
CM_ SG_ 48 FCWSomething "All bit set during fcw";
CM_ SG_ 48 StatusSomething "Some status changes when zeroing DTCs";
CM_ SG_ 208 TrqLim "Used in checksum calculation, Limit directional torque based on the number.";
CM_ SG_ 208 Checksum "Checksum calculated as a one-complement addition of LKAAngleRequest+LKADirection+Unkown, Zeros used to pad missing bits.";
CM_ SG_ 208 SET_X_02 "Bit 0 = Vibrate steering wheel., Bit 1 = Heartbeat";
CM_ SG_ 352 LkaDimLine "Not true, but follows lka steer direction.";
CM_ SG_ 352 NEW_SIGNAL_1 "Turned one. Got LKA service needed can this be the one?";
CM_ SG_ 640 ACC_Mode "Byte 6 bits 1-0 (bits 9-8 of the old 10-bit ACC_TractionRequest word). 0 = brake, 1 = coast, 2 = drive, same numbering as the V60 LongMode. Confirmed on 4 stock-ACC routes (7c7d3d5e5ff31d51 19/1a, 18eb05bab882ec44 1a/1b, ~1230 s ACC). The 0x160 ACC_AccelRequest value alone sorts the mode: below about -0.5 m/s2 brake, -0.5 to 0 coast, 0 and up drive, with hysteresis overlap.";
CM_ SG_ 640 ACC_TractionRequest "Byte 7, the traction value for ACC_Mode (was the low 8 bits of a 10-bit word with the mode on top). Unsigned in drive, signed in coast (0xEA = -22, engine drag), 0 in brake. Against the 0x160 ACC_AccelRequest (4 routes): drive = 86*a_req + 3 (r 0.93), coast = 54*a_req - 10 (r 0.73). Flat routes (grade within 2-3%) are tighter: drive about 92*a_req with ~0 offset (r 0.94-0.98), coast up to 93*a_req (r 0.85-0.97), close to the V60's 97/94. Hilly routes (5-6%) fit loosely (drive r 0.79-0.90, gain 63-78); adding a slope term changes nothing (at most 1 count per %), so the camera does not compensate grade in traction. Against measured aEgo: coast matches the V60 94*a - 9 (median error -0.02 to -0.04 m/s2), drive ~97*a + 35 (steady cruise needs 25-35 at any speed 20-120 km/h, because the camera requests about +0.3-0.5 m/s2 to hold speed). Medium-high confidence.";
CM_ SG_ 640 Byte_6_b7_6 "Always 3 (bits 15-14 of the word = 11), matching the V60 FSM4 brake word flags (0x8000 and 0x4000).";
CM_ SG_ 640 Byte_6_b5_3 "Bits 13-11 of the word, observed constant at 3 (011). Meaning unknown.";
CM_ SG_ 640 Byte_6_b2 "Bit 10 of the word. Clear whenever 0x270 byte 4 = 175 (11,700 of 11,708 frames in a manual drive; 10,540 of 10,544 in a highway ACC route), set otherwise. 175 is NOT ACC (seen with no ACC at all); most likely tied to openpilot being engaged, unproven. Explains the 0xD800 vs 0xDC00 floors seen in different routes.";
CM_ SG_ 640 SpeedTarget "SpeedTarget ACC (noisy bf starting acc Jumps from 0->252->0) Route 19: also behaves like a brake target, lower = more braking: median about 35 while ACC drives, about 0 while ACC brakes or holds, 252 with ACC off. Correlation with BrakePress0 during ACC braking only -0.34, so width and meaning are unconfirmed.";
CM_ BO_ 352 "0x160, camera to car (bus 2 -> relayed to bus 0), 50 Hz. Every 5th frame is a masked copy: the same frame with byte 0 & ~0x90, byte 2 & ~0xD5, byte 3 & ~0x40, byte 5 & ~0xD0 and byte 7 & ~0x80 (all 52,066 masked frames on 7 routes; the brake request bits survive). No counter or checksum: byte 6 bits 2-0 are a slow state (1/3/4/5), and the only full-range bytes are ACC_MeasuredAccel and ACC_AccelRequest. The signals cover all 64 bits, so a stock frame re-packs byte-identical.";
CM_ SG_ 352 ACC_BrakeRequest "UNCONFIRMED (medium-low). Set ~0.44 s before hydraulic pressure rises at both ACC braking events (586.3 s, 873.2 s). Not set on driver braking while moving. Also stays set at standstill with brake held. One 0.5 s false blip seen at 751 s with no braking. Also set in masked frames. Confirmed again in dashcam route (stock ACC stop 34-51 s) and 15 km/h route (decels at 110 s and 126 s): flag precedes hydraulic pressure and appears on ACC decel even without hydraulic braking. Route 19: 0.99 of samples while ACC brakes (0x1B0 byte 2 = 0xA5), 0.00 at ACC idle and in standstill hold. 5 routes: this is the HYDRAULIC brake request. In brake mode it agrees with BrakePress0 rising in 84-100% of frames, and pressure only rises with it set (median rise 28-40 with, 0 without). Never set outside 0x280 ACC_Mode = brake or with ACC off. Brake mode without it is engine braking only (two highway routes never set it). High confidence.";
CM_ SG_ 352 ACC_BrakeRequest_B "UNCONFIRMED. Same behaviour as ACC_BrakeRequest. Always set when ACC_BrakeRequest is set, and also sometimes alone (2270 frames). Route 19: it is the only one of the two set (1.00 of samples) during an ACC standstill hold, and 0.99 while ACC brakes.";
CM_ SG_ 352 ACC_AccelRequest "Byte 7 bits 6-0 (was NEW_SIGNAL_2 56|7@1+, same bits). The ACC acceleration request: (raw - 64) * ~0.08 m/s2, zero at 64. Braking side (5 routes incl. 00000008): 0.073-0.077 per count for firm requests, pooled fit 0.083; on flat routes 0.08 gives 0x280 traction gains of 90-94, matching the V60's 97/94. Leads measured aEgo by 0.2-0.4 s, sits on fixed values (raw 191/197 with bit 7) with ACC off, keeps falling through brake mode where traction is 0, and drive traction follows it at r 0.93. Looks like a 7-bit form of the V60 FSM3 ACC_AccelerationRequest (8-bit, 0.04). 4 stock-ACC routes, hardest request seen about -2 m/s2. Medium-high confidence.";
CM_ SG_ 352 Byte_7_b7 "Byte 7 bit 7. Always 1 in normal frames, 0 in the masked copies; likely a validity qualifier for ACC_AccelRequest.";
CM_ SG_ 352 ACC_MeasuredAccel "Byte 3 bits 2-0 + byte 4 (11 bits). MEASURED longitudinal acceleration, NOT a command: (raw - 1030) / ~225 m/s2 (fits 217-237 counts per m/s2 on 4 routes). Lags aEgo by 0.1-0.2 s and tracks it with ACC off too (r 0.87-0.95). This is what made the old Byte_4 sweep and the Byte_3 84 -> 82 drift during ACC braking (the high bits).";
CM_ SG_ 352 Byte_3_b7_3 "Byte 3 bits 7-3. Bit 6 is cleared in the masked copies (0x55 -> 0x15).";
CM_ SG_ 352 Byte_6_b2_0 "Byte 6 bits 2-0: 1, 3, 4 or 5, changing rarely (state, not a counter). Meaning unknown.";
CM_ SG_ 352 Byte_2_b4_0 "Byte 2 is 213 idle, 245 once ACC braking starts (only bit 5 differs). Replaces old NEW_SIGNAL_3 (7|24).";
CM_ SG_ 624 Byte_4 "Reads 0x87 or 0x00 with stock ACC engaged, so it is NOT the ACC engaged state. 0xAF (175) appears with no ACC at all (e.g. 4 stretches in a 2238 s manual drive) and begins before ACC is switched on, then continues after it ends; most likely tied to openpilot being engaged, unproven. Other values seen: 0x28 (40), 0x9F, 0xA7. Bit 10 of the 0x280 word (Byte_6_b2) is clear exactly when this reads 175.";
CM_ SG_ 528 LKA_State "0x210 byte 0 bit 2, 40 Hz, bus 0. Confirmed working as intended on the volvo_redlight branch. Seen in logs: on for the whole of a 1335 s manual drive and a highway route, never on in the 15 km/h set-speed route (likely LKA switched off for that drive). Follows the LKA enabled setting, not activity.";
CM_ SG_ 624 ACC_LeadDecelRaw "Signed 16-bit, -1 idle (about -230 steady with a lead in some logs). Goes strongly negative (to -3300 and lower) when a lead car ahead is braking, and stayed -1 during ACC own set-speed decels (-1.8 m/s2), so it is a lead-related decel demand, NOT the ACC decel request. Never positive. Low confidence. Route 19 (ACC active, gas off): correlates with measured acceleration, r = 0.67 at 0.3 s lag (the high byte carries it, adding the low byte changes nothing). Median -2539 while ACC brakes versus -236 at idle. Bytes 2 and 3 are one 16-bit value, not separate decel and traction fields. 4 routes: not -1 in 43-72% of moving ACC-off samples, ramps down about 1 s before ACC brakes and its peak does not match the braking achieved, so not an ACC command.";
CM_ SG_ 624 Byte_0 "Always 0";
CM_ SG_ 624 Byte_1 "Always 0";
CM_ SG_ 624 Byte_5 "0 or 2; 2 seen when throttle is on";
CM_ SG_ 624 Byte_6 "Always 0";
CM_ SG_ 624 Byte_7 "Always 0";
CM_ SG_ 640 Byte_0 "0x40, bit 3 sometimes set";
CM_ SG_ 864 ACC_DemandChangeFlag "10 Hz. Idle 164 (163 in manual). Under ACC it spikes high (~244-254) as ACC begins re-accelerating and low (0-21) when it begins decelerating. Event marker, not a request value. Medium confidence.";
CM_ SG_ 853 TargetSpeedOdo "Probably target speed odo";
CM_ SG_ 853 LaneMarkingsOdo "Bit 3=Left lane, Bit 2=Right lane, Bit 1=LKA on?, Bit 0=?";
CM_ SG_ 709 SpeedTargetACC "SpeedTargetACC";
CM_ SG_ 709 ACC_PropulsionFeedback "0x2C5 byte 7, ECM to camera (bus 0, echoed on bus 130), 16.7 Hz. Follows accelerator pedal (r~0.8). Pedal at zero: ~0 in manual driving, ~21 under ACC (ACC torque). Reads 0 during braking, ~25 at cruise, 160+ at +1.5 m/s2 (fit ~70*a+25). ECM output / feedback, NOT a request. Medium-low confidence.";
CM_ SG_ 224 rate_of_something "Seems to be some kind of torque rather than rate.";
CM_ SG_ 224 OneDuringDriving "Set to 1 when vehicle is rolling.";
CM_ SG_ 293 byte7 "Bit0=0 when gearshift in park, else 1";
CM_ SG_ 293 LKAActive "Bit0=0 when gear in park otherwise =1, Bit1=1 when LKA Active, 0 when not active. Bit2=? Bit3=?";
