CM_ SG_ 432 BrakeHold "Byte 2 bit 6. Set (0xE0/0xE1) while stock ACC holds the car at standstill.";
CM_ SG_ 432 BrakePress0 "Brake pressure. (byte0&3)<<8 | byte1. Rises under ACC braking with pedal flag off (peak ~108 at red-light event). Confirmed.";
CM_ SG_ 432 BrakePress1 "Brake pressure, second copy. (byte4&3)<<8 | byte5.";
CM_ SG_ 432 BrakeStatus "5 during ACC braking, 1 at standstill (observed). Other values not seen.";
CM_ BO_ 437 "0x1B5. Brake related, 10 ms, identical on bus 0 and bus 2 (camera sees it). Idle 2F FF C0 00 00 00 00 F8. Original Counter0-3 guesses (one per wheel?) not placed: bit layout unverified.";
CM_ SG_ 114 NEW_SIGNAL_1 "Jumped from 0 -> 120 during start. Makes triangle from time to time";
CM_ SG_ 608 NEW_SIGNAL_1 "Status?";
CM_ SG_ 608 NEW_SIGNAL_2 "Classification of object?";
CM_ SG_ 608 Distance "Distance to object in front. 1908 = no lead.";
CM_ SG_ 968 PassengerSeatBelt "1 = Seatbelt latched";
CM_ SG_ 968 DriverSeatBelt "1=Seatbelt latched";
CM_ BO_ 693 "0x2B5 ECM7. Brake-feedback candidate. Byte 2 is 0xF2 while stock ACC is braking (1.00 of samples on 3 routes), 0xB2 (0x9E parked/ACC off) otherwise incl. driver braking and coasting (<=0.001 false with ACC off). NOT sufficient: with ACC active and brake state idle it is also 0xF2 for 13-37% of samples (e.g. mild ACC slowdown at ~46 km/h, mostly >3 s from any 0xA5), so treat as necessary-not-sufficient. Edge leads the 0x1B0 byte 2 == 0xA5 edge by 90-460 ms. Also seen on bus 2 (camera). Observational only; nothing sent. The V60 ECM->FSM brake-feedback check suggests the camera compares such bytes with its own request. 0x2C3 (undefined here) byte 1 is 0x5C during ACC braking vs 0x54 otherwise, lag +100-200 ms, same pattern.";
CM_ BO_ 325 "0x145 ECM3. Byte 0 is the ACC standby-at-a-stop flag (observational): 0xA1 normally, 0xB9 from about 2.4-3.1 s into a standstill hold until the driver restarts it (wheel Resume, or the accelerator), then back to 0xA1 about 0.08 s after a successful Resume. Seen on 7 holds of 5.6-20.8 s on 4 routes, never during holds of 2.3 s or less (ACC resumes those by itself). Fits Volvo's documented ~3 s rule for Queue Assist. Not decoded further; byte 0 only.";
CM_ BO_ 480 "0x1E0 BCM0. Brake-feedback candidate. Byte 1 is 0x16 during ACC braking (0.92-0.94) vs 0x17 otherwise (<=0.002 false) on 3 routes. Lags the 0x1B0 A5 edge by 80-180 ms. Observational only.";
CM_ BO_ 176 "0xB0 ECM2. Byte 6 is 0xA3 during ACC braking (0.92-0.97) but also appears in ACC-active non-braking periods (0.35), so it is a state, not a clean brake confirmation. Leads the A5 edge by >1 s.";
CM_ BO_ 304 "0x130. Byte 6 tracks measured deceleration (r=0.91 driver braking, r=0.67 ACC braking) whatever causes it, so likely a continuous brake level or pressure value rather than an ACC flag. Observational only.";
VAL_ 64 GearShifter 0 "P" 1 "R" 2 "N" 3 "D" ;
VAL_ 432 BrakeStatus 1 "Standstill" 5 "ACC braking" ;
VAL_ 640 ACC_Mode 0 "Brake" 1 "Coast" 2 "Drive" ;%    
